<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scaliger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1262–1387</span> · Also known as della Scala family, Scaligeri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Scaliger, or della Scala, were a family who ruled Verona as lords from the 1260s to 1387. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastino-i-della-scala">Mastino I della Scala</a> was chosen leader of the commune in 1259, and under Cangrande I and Mastino II the family dominated north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, Treviso and for a time <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a>, Parma and Lucca. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a> ended their rule in 1387.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scaliger.jpg" alt="Scaliger" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xander · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stemma_della_Scala.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
